<figure id="S4.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T5.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 5</span>. </span><span id="S4.T5.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Results of <span id="S4.T5.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">single-document setup</span> (%, mean <math id="S4.T5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> SD with 95% CI) of ground-truth alignment rate for <span id="S4.T5.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">open-source LLMs</span> on <span id="S4.T5.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TREC 2020</span>. Providing helpful documents yields the highest ground-truth alignment rates across all models, while the Liar documents result in the lowest. The pattern of results is consistent across all three models, with cells shaded by mean value to indicate relative performance (darker shading corresponds to higher alignment rate).</span></figcaption>
